0..78 Comment "// A program reading a line through `std` and answering on one of two streams."
79..81 Comment "//"
82..157 Comment "// `main` is handed the ambient authority and opens the console from it, so"
158..235 Comment "// all three standard streams cross from that one capability. Nothing reaches"
236..275 Comment "// them through the ambient interfaces."
276..278 Comment "//"
279..357 Comment "// `read_line` keeps the line\'s newline, so `yes` arrives as `\"yes\\n\"`. `gandr"
358..436 Comment "// run answer.gandr` prints `agreed` on standard output for it, and `declined`"
437..476 Comment "// on standard error for anything else."
477..479 Comment "//"
480..556 Comment "// - see: `../../../library/std/src/console.gandr` — `print`, `eprint` and"
557..573 Comment "//   `read_line`"
574..627 Comment "// - see: #2970 — `std.authority` and `std.console`"
629..655 Comment "// `Authority`, `console`."
